MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1178431494}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e8c823e79b28e764ab0c934c38d1e97a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  slotName: {fileID: 1281481471}
  slotDescription: {fileID: 1702984982}
  Fungi:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 1392805154}
    button: {fileID: 1787281413}
    name: Fungi
    description: Fungi were once silent scavengers that thrived on decay, breaking
      down what was already dead and returning it to the ground. When imbalance spread
      across the land, they evolved into something more dangerous feeding not only
      on rot, but on weakness itself. Wherever battles leave scars, Fungi grow rapidly,
      releasing invisible spores that drain strength and slow resistance from anything
      nearby. They do not attack with force, but with persistence, spreading quietly,
      overwhelming defenses over time, and turning neglect into collapse. In this
      world, Fungi are a reminder that what is ignored for too long can become the
      hardest threat to remove.
  Virus:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 893199564}
    button: {fileID: 966196162}
    name: Virus
    description: Virus are the smallest enemies on the battlefield, yet the most
      deceptive. Invisible to the naked eye, they slip through defenses with ease,
      hijacking what they touch and forcing it to serve their own replication. Unlike
      other threats, Virus do not rely on strength or numbers alone they rely on
      speed, mutation, and surprise. Once they breach a line, they adapt rapidly,
      becoming harder to contain with every moment they survive. In this world, Virus
      embody the danger of unseen threats, proving that even the smallest enemy can
      cause the greatest collapse if left unchecked.
  Protozoa:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 1332664965}
    button: {fileID: 228220921}
    name: Protozoa
    description: "Protozoa are ancient lifeforms that existed long before the battlefield
      was ever formed, surviving through constant adaptation and cunning. Unlike
      mindless threats, they move with intention, sensing openings and exploiting
      weak points in defenses. Protozoa thrive in unstable environments, shifting
      their behavior when threatened and retreating only to strike again from a safer
      angle. Their strength lies not in raw power, but in intelligence and survival
      instinct, making them unpredictable opponents. In this world, Protozoa represent
      resilience through adaptation\u2014enemies that endure by learning how to survive
      every encounter."
  Helminth:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 1662908243}
    button: {fileID: 607798924}
    name: Helminth
    description: Helminth are massive parasitic creatures that advance slowly but
      relentlessly, burrowing through the battlefield with unwavering persistence.
      They do not rush their prey instead, they drain resources and stability over
      time, weakening defenses from within. Protected by thick layers and sheer endurance,
      Helminth are difficult to eliminate once they take hold. Their presence turns
      long battles into wars of attrition, where patience favors the enemy. In this
      world, Helminth symbolize the danger of prolonged neglect, showing that threats
      allowed to grow quietly can become nearly impossible to remove.
